      "name": "history-0-typed",
      "question": "Why?",
      "recognizedQuestion": "Why?",
      "answer": "Because a warp shares an instruction stream: the GPU issues an instruction to its active thread lanes together. If threads choose different branches, it executes each needed path with nonparticipating lanes masked off, so those lanes do no useful work during that path. The 32-thread size is NVIDIA’s architectural choice, not a fundamental requirement of parallel computing.",
